# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout}"
msgstr "Teoretikal na layout {#theoretical-layout}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "VQE's layout is simple:\n"
msgstr "Simple ang layout ng VQE:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare reference operators $U_R$\n"
msgstr "I-prepare ang reference operators na $U_R$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We start from the state $|0\\rangle$ and go to the reference state $|\\rho\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "Magsisimula tayo mula sa estado $|0\\rangle$ at pupunta sa reference state na $|\\rho\\rangle$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply the variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to create an ansatz $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$\n"
msgstr "I-apply ang variational form na $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ para lumikha ng ansatz na $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We go from the state $|\\rho\\rangle$ to $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})|\\rho\\rangle = |\\psi(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "Pupunta tayo mula sa estado $|\\rho\\rangle$ patungo sa $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})|\\rho\\rangle = |\\psi(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})\\rangle$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bootstrap at $i=0$ if we have a similar problem (typically found via classical simulation or sampling)\n"
msgstr "Mag-bootstrap sa $i=0$ kung mayroon kang katulad na problema (karaniwang nahahanap sa pamamagitan ng klasikal na simulation o sampling)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each optimizer will be bootstrapped differently, resulting in an initial set of parameter vectors $\\Theta_0 := \\\\{ {\\vec\\theta_{0,j} | j \\in \\mathcal{J}_\\text{opt}^0} \\\\}$ (for example, from an initial point $\\vec\\theta_0$).\n"
msgstr "Bawat optimizer ay mag-bo-bootstrap nang iba-iba, na magreresulta sa isang paunang hanay ng mga parameter vector na $\\Theta_0 := \\\\{ {\\vec\\theta_{0,j} | j \\in \\mathcal{J}_\\text{opt}^0} \\\\}$ (halimbawa, mula sa isang paunang punto $\\vec\\theta_0$).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate the cost function $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ for all prepared states on a quantum computer.\n"
msgstr "Suriin ang cost function na $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle$ para sa lahat ng inihanda na estado sa isang quantum computer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use a classical optimizer to select the next set of parameters $\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"
msgstr "Gumamit ng klasikal na optimizer para pumili ng susunod na hanay ng mga parameter na $\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat the process until convergence is reached.\n"
msgstr "Ulitin ang proseso hanggang maabot ang convergence.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is a simple classical optimization loop where we evaluate the cost function. Some optimizers may require multiple evaluations to calculate a gradient, determine the next iteration, or assess convergence.\n"
msgstr "Ito ay isang simpleng klasikal na optimization loop kung saan sinusuri natin ang cost function. Maaaring mangailangan ang ilang optimizer ng maraming evaluasyon para kalkulahin ang gradient, tukuyin ang susunod na iterasyon, o tasahin ang convergence.\n"

