msgid "Finally, we note that the function was evaluated 96 times in the process of optimization. That might be different from the number of optimization steps, since some optimizers require multiple function evaluations in a single step, such as when estimating a gradient.\n"
msgstr "Sa huli, dapat nating tandaan na 96 beses na sinuri ang function sa proseso ng optimization. Maaaring mag-iba ito mula sa bilang ng mga optimization step, dahil ang ilang optimizer ay nangangailangan ng maraming evaluasyon ng function sa isang hakbang, tulad ng kapag tinatantiya ang gradient.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Subspace Search VQE (SSVQE) {#subspace-search-vqe-ssvqe}"
msgstr "Subspace Search VQE (SSVQE) {#subspace-search-vqe-ssvqe}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[SSVQE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.09434) is a variant of VQE that allows obtaining the first $k$ eigenvalues of an observable $\\hat{H}$ with eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, where $N\\geq k$. Without loss of generality, we assume that $\\lambda_0<\\lambda_1<...<\\lambda_{N-1}$. SSVQE introduces a new idea by adding weights to help prioritize optimizing for the term with the largest weight.\n"
msgstr "Ang [SSVQE](https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.09434) ay isang variant ng VQE na nagpapahintulot sa pagkuha ng unang $k$ eigenvalue ng isang observable na $\\hat{H}$ na may mga eigenvalue na $\\{\\lambda_0, \\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$, kung saan $N\\geq k$. Nang walang pagkawala ng pangkalahatan, ipinapalagay natin na $\\lambda_0<\\lambda_1<...<\\lambda_{N-1}$. Nagpapakilala ang SSVQE ng bagong ideya sa pamamagitan ng pagdaragdag ng mga timbang upang matulungang bigyang-priyoridad ang pag-optimize para sa term na may pinakamalaking timbang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing how subspace-search VQE uses the components of variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-ssvqe.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Isang diagram na nagpapakita kung paano ginagamit ng subspace-search VQE ang mga component ng variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-ssvqe.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To implement this algorithm, we need $k$ mutually orthogonal reference states $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, meaning $\\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ for $j,l<k$. These states can be constructed using Pauli operators. The cost function of this algorithm is then:\n"
msgstr "Para maipatupad ang algorithm na ito, kailangan natin ng $k$ na magkaparehong ortogonal na reference state na $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, ibig sabihin $\\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ para sa $j,l<k$. Ang mga estadong ito ay maaaring itayo gamit ang mga Pauli operator. Ang cost function ng algorithm na ito ay:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{\\theta})\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{\\theta})\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\rho_j | U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})\\hat{H} U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\rho_j | U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})\\hat{H} U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $w_j$ is an arbitrary positive number such that if $j<l<k$ then $w_j>w_l$, and $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})$ is the user-defined variational form.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $w_j$ ay isang arbitraryong positibong numero na kung $j<l<k$ ay $w_j>w_l$, at ang $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})$ ay ang variational form na tinukoy ng gumagamit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The SSVQE algorithm relies on the fact that eigenstates corresponding to different eigenvalues are mutually orthogonal. Specifically, the inner product of $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle$ and $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l\\rangle$ can be expressed as:\n"
msgstr "Ang SSVQE algorithm ay nakasalalay sa katotohanang ang mga eigenstate na naaayon sa iba't ibang eigenvalue ay magkaparehong ortogonal. Partikular, ang inner product ng $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle$ at $U_V(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l\\rangle$ ay maaaring ipahayag bilang:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\rho_j | U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l \\rangle\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\rho_j | U_{V}^{\\dagger}(\\vec{\\theta})U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_l \\rangle\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\langle \\rho_j | I |\\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\langle \\rho_j | I |\\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\delta_{jl}\n"
msgstr "& = \\delta_{jl}\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first equality holds because $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})$ is a quantum operator and is therefore unitary. The last equality holds because of the orthogonality of the reference states $|\\rho_j\\rangle$. The fact that orthogonality is preserved through unitary transformations is deeply related to the principle of conservation of information, as expressed in quantum information science. Under this view, non-unitary transformations represent processes where information is either lost or injected.\n"
msgstr "Ang unang pagkakapantay-pantay ay totoo dahil ang $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})$ ay isang quantum operator at samakatuwid ay unitary. Ang huling pagkakapantay-pantay ay totoo dahil sa ortogonalidad ng mga reference state na $|\\rho_j\\rangle$. Ang katotohanang napapanatili ang ortogonalidad sa pamamagitan ng mga unitary transformation ay malalim na nauugnay sa prinsipyo ng pangangalaga ng impormasyon, gaya ng ipinapahayag sa quantum information science. Sa pananaw na ito, ang mga non-unitary transformation ay kumakatawan sa mga proseso kung saan ang impormasyon ay nawawala o naiiniksyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Weights $w_j$ help ensure that all the states are eigenstates. If the weights are sufficiently different, the term with the largest weight (that is, $w_0$) will be given priority during optimization over the others. As a result, the resulting state $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_0 \\rangle$ will become the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_0$. Because $\\{ U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$ are mutually orthogonal, the remaining states will be orthogonal to it and, therefore, contained in the subspace corresponding to the eigenvalues $\\{\\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Tinutulungan ng mga timbang $w_j$ na matiyak na lahat ng estado ay mga eigenstate. Kung sapat na magkaiba ang mga timbang, ang term na may pinakamalaking timbang (ibig sabihin, $w_0$) ay mabibigyan ng priyoridad sa panahon ng optimization kaysa sa iba. Bilang resulta, ang resultang estado $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_0 \\rangle$ ay magiging eigenstate na naaayon sa $\\lambda_0$. Dahil ang $\\{ U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$ ay magkaparehong ortogonal, ang natitirang mga estado ay magiging ortogonal dito at, samakatuwid, nakapaloob sa subspace na naaayon sa mga eigenvalue na $\\{\\lambda_1,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying the same argument to the rest of the terms, the next priority would then be the term with weight $w_1$, so $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_1 \\rangle$ would be the eigenstate corresponding to $\\lambda_1$, and the other terms would be contained in the eigenspace of $\\{\\lambda_2,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Sa paglalapat ng parehong argumento sa natitirang mga term, ang susunod na priyoridad ay ang term na may timbang $w_1$, kaya ang $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_1 \\rangle$ ay magiging eigenstate na naaayon sa $\\lambda_1$, at ang ibang mga term ay mananatili sa eigenspace ng $\\{\\lambda_2,...,\\lambda_{N-1}\\}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By reasoning inductively, we deduce that $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j \\rangle$ will be an approximate eigenstate of $\\lambda_j$ for $0\\leq j < k$.\n"
msgstr "Sa pamamagitan ng inductive reasoning, natutukoy natin na ang $U_{V}(\\vec{\\theta})|\\rho_j \\rangle$ ay magiging isang tinatayang eigenstate ng $\\lambda_j$ para sa $0\\leq j < k$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout-1}"
msgstr "Teoretikal na layout {#theoretical-layout-1}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SSVQE's can be summarized as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang SSVQE ay maaaring ibuod tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare several reference states by applying a unitary U_R to k different computational basis states\n"
msgstr "Maghanda ng ilang reference state sa pamamagitan ng pag-apply ng unitary U_R sa k iba't ibang computational basis state\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "This algorithm requires the usage of $k$ mutually orthogonal reference states $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, such that $\\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ for $j,l<k$.\n"
msgstr "Ang algorithm na ito ay nangangailangan ng paggamit ng $k$ magkaparehong ortogonal na reference state na $\\{ |\\rho_j\\rangle \\}_{j=0}^{k-1}$, tulad na $\\langle \\rho_j | \\rho_l \\rangle = \\delta_{jl}$ para sa $j,l<k$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply the variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to each reference state, resulting in the following ansatz $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"
msgstr "I-apply ang variational form na $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ sa bawat reference state, na nagbubunga sa sumusunod na ansatz na $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bootstrap at $i=0$ if a similar problem is available (usually found via classical simulation or sampling).\n"
msgstr "Mag-bootstrap sa $i=0$ kung mayroon kang katulad na problema (karaniwang nahahanap sa pamamagitan ng klasikal na simulation o sampling).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate the cost function $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ for all prepared states on a quantum computer.\n"
msgstr "Suriin ang cost function na $C(\\vec\\theta_{i,j}) := \\sum_{j=0}^{k-1} w_j \\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ para sa lahat ng inihanda na estado sa isang quantum computer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "This can be separated into calculating the expectation value for an observable $\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ and multiplying that result by $w_j$.\n"
msgstr "Maaari itong hatiin sa pagkalkula ng expectation value para sa isang observable na $\\langle \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi_{j}(\\vec{\\theta}) \\rangle$ at pagpaparami ng resultang iyon sa $w_j$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Afterward, the cost function returns the sum of all weighted expectation values.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos, ibinabalik ng cost function ang kabuuan ng lahat ng weighted expectation value.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use a classical optimizer to determine the next set of parameters $\\Theta_{i+1}$.\n"
