# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation {#implementation-1}"
msgstr "Implementasyon {#implementation-1}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this implementation, we'll create a function for an overlap penalty. This penalty will be used in the cost function at each iteration. This process will be repeated for each excited state\n"
msgstr "Para sa implementasyong ito, gagawa tayo ng function para sa isang overlap penalty. Gagamitin ang penalty na ito sa cost function sa bawat iterasyon. Ang prosesong ito ay uulitin para sa bawat excited state.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/extracted-outputs/9d368de5-d512-4fe8-8842-9c735944b22b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/extracted-outputs/9d368de5-d512-4fe8-8842-9c735944b22b-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we'll set up a function that calculates the state fidelity -- a percentage of overlap between two states that we'll use as a penalty for VQD:\n"
msgstr "Una, mag-se-set up tayo ng function na nagkalkula ng state fidelity — isang porsyento ng overlap sa pagitan ng dalawang estado na gagamitin natin bilang penalty para sa VQD:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It's time to write VQD's cost function. As before when we calculated only the ground state, we will determine the lowest energy state using the Estimator primitive. However, as described above, we will now add a penalty term to ensure orthogonality of higher-energy states. That is, for each new excited state, a penalty is added for any overlap between the current variational state and the lower-energy eigenstates already found.\n"
msgstr "Oras na para isulat ang cost function ng VQD. Gaya ng dati nang kinalkula natin ang ground state lamang, tutukuyin natin ang pinakamababang energy state gamit ang Estimator primitive. Gayunpaman, gaya ng inilarawan sa itaas, magdadagdag na tayo ng penalty term para matiyak ang ortogonalidad ng mga higher-energy state. Ibig sabihin, para sa bawat bagong excited state, idinaragdag ang isang penalty para sa anumang overlap sa pagitan ng kasalukuyang variational state at ng mga lower-energy eigenstate na nahanap na.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note especially that the cost function above refers to the `calculate_overlaps` function, which actually creates a new quantum circuit. If we want to run on real hardware, that new circuit must also be transpiled, hopefully in an optimal way, to run on the backend we select. Note that transpilation has been built in to the `calculate_overlaps` or `cost_func_vqd` functions. Feel free to try modifying the code yourself to build in this additional (and conditional) transpilation - but this will also be done for you in the next lesson.\n"
msgstr "Dapat pansinin na ang cost function sa itaas ay tumutukoy sa function na `calculate_overlaps`, na lumilikha ng bagong quantum circuit. Kung gusto nating patakbuhin sa tunay na hardware, ang bagong circuit na iyon ay kailangang i-transpile rin, sana sa pinakamainam na paraan, para patakbuhin sa backend na ating pipiliin. Tandaan na ang transpilation ay hindi pa nakabuilt-in sa mga function na `calculate_overlaps` o `cost_func_vqd`. Huwag mag-atubiling subukan na baguhin ang code mismo para isama ang karagdagang (at conditional) transpilation na ito — ngunit gagawin din ito para sa iyo sa susunod na aralin.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this lesson, we will run the VQD algorithm using the Statevector Sampler and Statevector Estimator:\n"
msgstr "Sa araling ito, patatakbuhin natin ang VQD algorithm gamit ang Statevector Sampler at Statevector Estimator:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will introduce an observable to be estimated. In the next lesson we will add some physical context to this, like the excited state of a molecule. It may be helpful to think of this observable as the Hamiltonian of a system that can have excited states, even though this observable has not been chosen to match any particular molecule or atom.\n"
msgstr "Magpapakilala tayo ng isang observable na ie-estimate. Sa susunod na aralin, magdadagdag tayo ng ilang pisikal na konteksto dito, tulad ng excited state ng isang molekula. Maaaring makatulong na isiping ang observable na ito bilang Hamiltonian ng isang sistema na maaaring magkaroon ng mga excited state, kahit na ang observable na ito ay hindi pinili para tumugma sa anumang partikular na molekula o atom.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, we set the total number of states we wish to calculate (ground state and excited states, k), and the penalties (betas) for overlap between statevectors that should be orthogonal. The consequences of choosing betas to be too high or too low will be explored a bit in the next lesson. For now, we will simply use those provided below. We will start by using all zeros as our parameters. In your own calculations, you may want to use more clever starting parameters based on your knowledge of the system or on previous calculations.\n"
msgstr "Dito, itinatakda natin ang kabuuang bilang ng mga estado na gustong kalkulahin (ground state at excited state, k), at ang mga parusa (betas) para sa overlap sa pagitan ng mga statevector na dapat na ortogonal. Ang mga kahihinatnan ng pagpili ng masyadong mataas o masyadong mababang betas ay matutuklasan nang kaunti sa susunod na aralin. Sa ngayon, gagamit lang tayo ng mga ibinigay sa ibaba. Magsisimula tayo sa paggamit ng lahat ng zero bilang ating mga parameter. Sa iyong sariling mga kalkulasyon, maaaring gusto mong gumamit ng mas matalinong panimulang parameter batay sa iyong kaalaman sa sistema o sa mga nakaraang kalkulasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now run the calculation:\n"
msgstr "Maaari na tayong patakbuhin ang kalkulasyon:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The values we obtained from the cost function are approximately -6.00, 4.02, and 5.61. The important thing about these results is that the function values are increasing. If we had obtained a first excited state that is lower in energy than our initial, unconstrained calculation of the ground state, that would have indicated an error somewhere in our code.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga halagang nakuha namin mula sa cost function ay humigit-kumulang -6.00, 4.02, at 5.61. Ang mahalagang bagay tungkol sa mga resultang ito ay ang pagtaas ng mga function value. Kung nakakuha tayo ng unang excited state na mas mababa sa enerhiya kaysa sa ating paunang, unconstrained na kalkulasyon ng ground state, ito ay magpapahiwatig ng isang pagkakamali sa ating code.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The values of x are the parameters that yielded a statevector corresponding to each of these costs (energies).\n"
msgstr "Ang mga halaga ng x ay ang mga parameter na nagbunga ng statevector na naaayon sa bawat isa sa mga cost (enerhiya) na ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we note that all three minimizations converged to within the default tolerance of the classical optimizer (here COBYLA). They required 131, 110, and 90 function evaluations, respectively.\n"
msgstr "Sa huli, dapat nating tandaan na ang lahat ng tatlong minimization ay nagconverge sa loob ng default na toleransya ng klasikal na optimizer (dito COBYLA). Nangangailangan ang mga ito ng 131, 110, at 90 na evaluasyon ng function, ayon sa pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum Sampling Regression (QSR) {#quantum-sampling-regression-qsr}"
msgstr "Quantum Sampling Regression (QSR) {#quantum-sampling-regression-qsr}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One of the main issues with VQE is the multiple calls to a quantum computer that are required to obtain the parameters for each step, for example, $k$, $k-1$, and so on. This is especially problematic when access to quantum devices is queued. While a [`Session`](/guides/run-jobs-session) can be used to group multiple iterative calls, an alternative approach is to use sampling. By utilizing more classical resources, we can complete the full optimization process in a single call. This is where [Quantum Sampling Regression](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.02338) comes into play. Since access to quantum computers is still a low-offer/high-demand commodity, we find this trade-off to be both possible and convenient for many current studies. This approach harnesses all available classical capabilities while still capturing many of the inner workings and intrinsic properties of quantum computations that do not appear in simulation.\n"
msgstr "Isa sa mga pangunahing isyu sa VQE ay ang maraming tawag sa isang quantum computer na kinakailangan para makuha ang mga parameter para sa bawat hakbang, halimbawa, $k$, $k-1$, at iba pa. Lalo itong nagiging problema kapag ang access sa mga quantum device ay nasa pila. Habang maaaring gamitin ang [`Session`](/guides/run-jobs-session) para pagsamahin ang maraming iteratibong tawag, ang isang alternatibong pamamaraan ay ang paggamit ng sampling. Sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng mas maraming klasikal na mapagkukunan, maaari nating makumpleto ang buong proseso ng optimization sa isang tawag lamang. Dito pumapasok ang [Quantum Sampling Regression](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.02338). Dahil ang access sa mga quantum computer ay isang mababang-alok/mataas-demand na kalakal, natutuklasan namin na ang trade-off na ito ay parehong posible at maginhawa para sa maraming kasalukuyang pag-aaral. Ang pamamaraang ito ay gumagamit ng lahat ng magagamit na klasikal na kakayahan habang nino-capture pa rin ang marami sa mga panloob na mekanismo at likas na katangian ng mga quantum computation na hindi lumalabas sa simulation.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram showing how QSR uses the components of a variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-qsr.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Isang diagram na nagpapakita kung paano ginagamit ng QSR ang mga component ng variational algorithm.](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/instances-and-extensions/instances-qsr.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The idea behind QSR is that the cost function $C(\\theta) := \\langle \\psi(\\theta) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\theta)\\rangle$ can be expressed as a Fourier series in the following manner:\n"
msgstr "Ang ideya sa likod ng QSR ay ang cost function na $C(\\theta) := \\langle \\psi(\\theta) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\theta)\\rangle$ ay maaaring ipahayag bilang isang Fourier series sa sumusunod na paraan:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& := \\langle \\psi(\\theta) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\theta)\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& := \\langle \\psi(\\theta) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\theta)\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& := a_0 + \\sum_{k=1}^S[a_k\\cos(k\\theta)+ b_k\\sin(k\\theta)] \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& := a_0 + \\sum_{k=1}^S[a_k\\cos(k\\theta)+ b_k\\sin(k\\theta)] \\\\[1mm]\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Depending on the periodicity and bandwidth of the original function, the set $S$ may be finite or infinite. For the purposes of this discussion, we will assume it is infinite. The next step is to sample the cost function $C(\\theta)$ multiple times in order to obtain the Fourier coefficients $\\{a_0, a_k, b_k\\}_{k=1}^S$. Specifically, since we have $2S+1$ unknowns, we will need to sample the cost function $2S+1$ times.\n"
msgstr "Depende sa periodicity at bandwidth ng orihinal na function, ang set na $S$ ay maaaring finite o infinite. Para sa layunin ng talakayan na ito, ipapalagay natin na ito ay infinite. Ang susunod na hakbang ay ang pag-sample ng cost function na $C(\\theta)$ nang maraming beses para makuha ang mga Fourier coefficient na $\\{a_0, a_k, b_k\\}_{k=1}^S$. Partikular, dahil mayroon kaming $2S+1$ na hindi kilala, kakailanganing i-sample ang cost function nang $2S+1$ beses.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we then sample the cost function for $2S+1$ parameter values $\\{\\theta_1,...,\\theta_{2S+1}\\}$, we can obtain the following system:\n"
msgstr "Kung mag-sample tayo ng cost function para sa $2S+1$ na halaga ng parameter na $\\{\\theta_1,...,\\theta_{2S+1}\\}$, maaari tayong makakuha ng sumusunod na sistema:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & \\cos(\\theta_1) & \\sin(\\theta_1) & \\cos(2\\theta_1) & ... & \\sin(S\\theta_1) \\\\\n"
"1 & \\cos(\\theta_2) & \\sin(\\theta_2) & \\cos(2\\theta_2) & \\cdots & \\sin(S\\theta_2)\\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\\n"
"1 & \\cos(\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\sin(\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\cos(2\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\cdots & \\sin(S\\theta_{2S+1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} a_0 \\\\ a_1 \\\\ b_1 \\\\ a_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ b_S \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} C(\\theta_1) \\\\ C(\\theta_2) \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ C(\\theta_{2S+1}) \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & \\cos(\\theta_1) & \\sin(\\theta_1) & \\cos(2\\theta_1) & ... & \\sin(S\\theta_1) \\\\\n"
"1 & \\cos(\\theta_2) & \\sin(\\theta_2) & \\cos(2\\theta_2) & \\cdots & \\sin(S\\theta_2)\\\\\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\\n"
"1 & \\cos(\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\sin(\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\cos(2\\theta_{2S+1}) & \\cdots & \\sin(S\\theta_{2S+1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} a_0 \\\\ a_1 \\\\ b_1 \\\\ a_2 \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ b_S \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} C(\\theta_1) \\\\ C(\\theta_2) \\\\ \\vdots \\\\ C(\\theta_{2S+1}) \\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "that we'll rewrite as\n"
msgstr "na isusulat natin bilang\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Fa=c.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Fa=c.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In practice, this system is generally not consistent because the cost function values $c$ are not exact. Therefore, it is usually a good idea to normalize them by multiplying them by $F^\\dagger$ on the left, which results in:\n"
msgstr "Sa practice, ang sistemang ito ay kadalasang hindi consistent dahil ang mga halaga ng cost function na $c$ ay hindi eksaktong tumpak. Samakatuwid, kadalasang magandang ideya na i-normalize ang mga ito sa pamamagitan ng pagpaparami ng $F^\\dagger$ sa kaliwa, na nagbubunga ng:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"F^\\dagger Fa = F^\\dagger c.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"F^\\dagger Fa = F^\\dagger c.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This new system is always consistent, and its solution is a least-squares solution to the original problem. If we have $k$ parameters instead of just one, and each parameter $\\theta^i$ has its own $S_i$ for $i \\in {1,...,k}$, then the total number of samples required is:\n"
msgstr "Ang bagong sistemang ito ay palaging consistent, at ang solusyon nito ay isang least-squares na solusyon sa orihinal na problema. Kung mayroon tayong $k$ na parameter sa halip na isa lamang, at ang bawat parameter na $\\theta^i$ ay may sariling $S_i$ para sa $i \\in {1,...,k}$, ang kabuuang bilang ng mga kinakailangang sample ay:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"T=\\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_i+1)\\leq \\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_{max}+1) = (2S_{max}+1)^n,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"T=\\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_i+1)\\leq \\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_{max}+1) = (2S_{max}+1)^n,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $S_{\\max} = \\max_i(S_i)$. Furthermore, adjusting $S_{\\max}$ as a tunable parameter (instead of inferring it) opens up new possibilities, such as:\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $S_{\\max} = \\max_i(S_i)$. Higit pa rito, ang pag-aayos ng $S_{\\max}$ bilang isang tuneable parameter (sa halip na i-infer ito) ay nagbubukas ng mga bagong posibilidad, tulad ng:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Over-sampling** to improve accuracy.\n"
msgstr "**Over-sampling** para mapabuti ang katumpakan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Under-sampling** to boost performance by reducing runtime overhead or eliminating local minima.\n"
msgstr "**Under-sampling** para palakasin ang performance sa pamamagitan ng pagbabawas ng runtime overhead o pag-aalis ng mga local minima.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Theoretical layout {#theoretical-layout-3}"
msgstr "Teoretikal na layout {#theoretical-layout-3}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "QSR's layout can be summarized as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang layout ng QSR ay maaaring ibuod tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare reference operators $U_R$.\n"
msgstr "Maghanda ng reference operators na $U_R$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll go from the state $|0\\rangle$ to the reference state $|\\rho\\rangle$\n"
msgstr "Pupunta tayo mula sa estado $|0\\rangle$ patungo sa reference state na $|\\rho\\rangle$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply the  variational form $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ to create an ansatz $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"
msgstr "I-apply ang variational form na $U_V(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$ para lumikha ng ansatz na $U_A(\\vec\\theta_{i,j})$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Determine the bandwidth associated with each parameter in the ansatz. An upper bound is sufficient.\n"
msgstr "Tukuyin ang bandwidth na nauugnay sa bawat parameter sa ansatz. Sapat ang isang upper bound.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bootstrap at $i=0$ if we have a similar problem (typically found by classical simulation or sampling).\n"
msgstr "I-sample ang cost function na $C(\\vec\\theta) := a_0 + \\sum_{k=1}^S[a_k\\cos(k\\theta)+ b_k\\sin(k\\theta)]$ nang hindi bababa sa $T$ beses.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample the cost function $C(\\vec\\theta) := a_0 + \\sum_{k=1}^S[a_k\\cos(k\\theta)+ b_k\\sin(k\\theta)]$ at least $T$ times.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$T=\\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_i+1)\\leq \\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_{max}+1) = (2S_{max}+1)^n$\n"
msgstr "$T=\\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_i+1)\\leq \\prod_{i=1}^k(2S_{max}+1) = (2S_{max}+1)^n$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Decide whether to over-sample/under-sample to balance speed vs accuracy by adjusting $T$.\n"
msgstr "Magpasya kung mag-over-sample o mag-under-sample para balansehin ang bilis kumpara sa katumpakan sa pamamagitan ng pag-aayos ng $T$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute the Fourier coefficients from the samples (that is, solve the normalized linear system of equations).\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang mga Fourier coefficient mula sa mga sample (ibig sabihin, lutasin ang normalized na linear system ng mga equation).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solve for the global minimum of the resulting regression function on a classical machine.\n"
msgstr "Lutasin ang pandaigdigang minimum ng resultang regression function sa isang klasikal na makina.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Buod {#summary}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With this lesson, you learned about multiple variational instances available:\n"
msgstr "Sa araling ito, natuto ka tungkol sa maraming variational instance na magagamit:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "General layout\n"
msgstr "Pangkalahatang layout\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introducing weights and penalties to adjust a cost function\n"
msgstr "Pagpapakilala ng mga timbang at parusa para ayusin ang cost function\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exploring under-sampling vs over-sampling to trade-off speed vs accuracy\n"
msgstr "Pagtuklas ng under-sampling kumpara sa over-sampling para i-trade-off ang bilis kumpara sa katumpakan\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These ideas can be adapted to form a custom variational algorithm that fits your problem. We encourage you to share your results with the community. The next lesson will explore how to use a variational algorithm to solve an application.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga ideyang ito ay maaaring iangkop para makabuo ng custom variational algorithm na angkop sa iyong problema. Hinihikayat namin kayo na ibahagi ang inyong mga resulta sa komunidad. Tutuklasin ng susunod na aralin kung paano gamitin ang variational algorithm para malutas ng isang application.\n"
